⚙️ Common Map Methods

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 put()

Adds key-value pair.

```java
map.put(101, "John");
```

---

🔹 get()

Returns value using key.

```java
System.out.println(map.get(101));
```

---

🔹 remove()

Removes key-value pair.

```java
map.remove(101);
```

---

🔹 containsKey()

Checks whether key exists.

```java
map.containsKey(102);
```

---

🔹 containsValue()

Checks whether value exists.

```java
map.containsValue("Java");
```

---

🔹 keySet()

Returns all keys.

```java
System.out.println(map.keySet());
```

---

🔹 values()

Returns all values.

```java
System.out.println(map.values());
```

---

🔹 entrySet()

Returns key-value entries.

```java
for (Map.Entry<Integer, String> entry : map.entrySet()) {

    System.out.println(
            entry.getKey() + " : " +
            entry.getValue());
}
```

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📊 HashMap vs LinkedHashMap vs TreeMap

| Feature            | HashMap    | LinkedHashMap            | TreeMap        |
| ------------------ | ---------- | ------------------------ | -------------- |
| Order              | ❌ No       | ✔ Insertion Order        | ✔ Sorted Order |
| Null Key           | ✔ One      | ✔ One                    | ❌ No           |
| Duplicate Values   | ✔ Yes      | ✔ Yes                    | ✔ Yes          |
| Performance        | Fastest    | Fast                     | Slower         |
| Internal Structure | Hash Table | Hash Table + Linked List | Red-Black Tree |

---

🎯 When to Use Which?

| Requirement               | Best Choice   |
| ------------------------- | ------------- |
| Fast Lookup               | HashMap       |
| Preserve Insertion Order  | LinkedHashMap |
| Automatically Sorted Keys | TreeMap       |

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Assuming HashMap preserves order

❌ Using null key in TreeMap

```java
TreeMap<Integer, String> map =
        new TreeMap<>();

map.put(null, "Java");
```

👉 Throws `NullPointerException`

---

❌ Forgetting that keys must be unique

